WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.083
(slow ambient music)

00:00:06.030 --> 00:00:09.160
- [Narrator] Restoring an item
back to its original state

00:00:09.160 --> 00:00:12.210
is a tedious and delicate process.

00:00:12.210 --> 00:00:15.890
Add a high price point, and
the stakes are even higher.

00:00:15.890 --> 00:00:20.330
Watch 10 restoration experts
transform designer goods

00:00:20.330 --> 00:00:22.920
such as Sharpie-stained Chanel bags,

00:00:22.920 --> 00:00:25.120
dog-bitten Louboutin shoes,

00:00:25.120 --> 00:00:28.173
and worn out Louis Vuitton
wallets back to new.

00:00:29.610 --> 00:00:31.660
Each artisan has their own way

00:00:31.660 --> 00:00:33.793
of restoring these luxury goods.

00:00:36.780 --> 00:00:39.830
Gerry Gallagher has been
repairing luxury handbags

00:00:39.830 --> 00:00:41.960
for over 30 years.

00:00:41.960 --> 00:00:46.960
This $3,000 Chanel GST was
accidentally burned by a candle.

00:00:51.930 --> 00:00:53.940
Gerry replaces the damaged leather

00:00:53.940 --> 00:00:57.203
on the back pocket of the
bag with caviar leather.

00:01:02.550 --> 00:01:04.160
This is the same type of leather

00:01:04.160 --> 00:01:05.903
it was originally made with.

00:01:08.830 --> 00:01:11.310
Once the burned section is replaced,

00:01:11.310 --> 00:01:13.720
Gerry stitches the bag back together...

00:01:13.720 --> 00:01:15.850
Making sure the sewing needle falls

00:01:15.850 --> 00:01:18.097
into the original stitch holes.

00:01:18.097 --> 00:01:21.180
(slow ambient music)

00:01:43.640 --> 00:01:47.053
Rio is the owner of Kim's
Shoe and Bag Repair.

00:01:48.090 --> 00:01:51.313
He is restoring a pair
of Chanel ballet flats.

00:01:53.150 --> 00:01:56.393
He starts by removing the
heel plates with an opener.

00:02:00.160 --> 00:02:03.493
Then he makes new rubber
soles and glues them on.

00:02:07.900 --> 00:02:12.104
The suede on the shoes has
faded, so it is being redyed.

00:02:12.104 --> 00:02:15.187
(slow ambient music)

00:02:25.540 --> 00:02:29.523
Handbag Clinic restores
designer handbags and shoes.

00:02:31.150 --> 00:02:35.113
This white Chanel GST was
drawn on with Sharpie.

00:02:36.960 --> 00:02:39.520
Chloe, an artisan at Handbag Clinic,

00:02:39.520 --> 00:02:42.380
starts by using a special ink remover

00:02:42.380 --> 00:02:44.382
to contain the spread of the ink.

00:02:44.382 --> 00:02:47.465
(slow ambient music)

00:02:54.030 --> 00:02:55.890
She then color matches paint

00:02:55.890 --> 00:02:57.913
to the original color of the bag.

00:03:01.120 --> 00:03:04.400
Color matching is important
for blending the restored parts

00:03:04.400 --> 00:03:05.453
with the original.

00:03:08.990 --> 00:03:11.210
Chloe airbrushes it on lightly,

00:03:11.210 --> 00:03:14.432
ensuring that the texture of
the leather is maintained.

00:03:14.432 --> 00:03:17.515
(slow ambient music)

00:03:25.250 --> 00:03:29.010
Rago Brothers Shoe &amp; Leather
Repair restores shoes

00:03:29.010 --> 00:03:30.890
and leather goods.

00:03:30.890 --> 00:03:35.253
These $1,000 Louboutins were
badly chewed up by a dog.

00:03:38.350 --> 00:03:40.400
The team removes and rebuilds

00:03:40.400 --> 00:03:42.568
the entire upper part of the shoe.

00:03:42.568 --> 00:03:45.651
(slow ambient music)

00:03:54.540 --> 00:03:56.810
They heat up new patent leather

00:03:56.810 --> 00:03:59.020
so that it becomes more malleable

00:03:59.020 --> 00:04:01.963
and stretch it over the
upper part of the shoe.

00:04:04.980 --> 00:04:07.154
Then they reattach the platform.

00:04:07.154 --> 00:04:10.237
(slow ambient music)

00:04:19.120 --> 00:04:21.640
Heath Potter is a professional cobbler

00:04:21.640 --> 00:04:24.420
and a co-founder of Potter &amp; Sons.

00:04:24.420 --> 00:04:26.800
The owner of these Ferragamo loafers

00:04:26.800 --> 00:04:28.573
wore the soles all the way through.

00:04:33.340 --> 00:04:37.263
Heath replaces the outsole
with German pit-tanned leather.

00:04:38.380 --> 00:04:40.833
It's long-lasting and waterproof.

00:04:46.900 --> 00:04:49.840
To finish the process,
he stitches the shoes

00:04:49.840 --> 00:04:51.773
and puts them onto a press.

00:05:03.230 --> 00:05:07.443
Vincent Rao Jr. is the owner
of Vince's Village Cobbler.

00:05:08.570 --> 00:05:10.440
The famous red-painted bottoms

00:05:10.440 --> 00:05:12.854
of these Louboutins have worn out.

00:05:12.854 --> 00:05:15.937
(slow ambient music)

00:05:21.840 --> 00:05:24.740
Vincent glues on a rubber sole protector

00:05:24.740 --> 00:05:26.943
to add the red color back on.

00:05:29.330 --> 00:05:33.051
It will last much longer
than the original red paint.

00:05:33.051 --> 00:05:36.134
(slow ambient music)

00:05:43.550 --> 00:05:45.790
Daniel James from Handbag Clinic

00:05:45.790 --> 00:05:48.823
is restoring a Louis Vuitton vanity case.

00:05:50.390 --> 00:05:54.260
The interior lining has
deteriorated from years of use.

00:05:54.260 --> 00:05:57.343
(slow ambient music)

00:06:03.500 --> 00:06:06.230
He makes patterns using the old pieces

00:06:06.230 --> 00:06:09.020
and replaces them with pigskin leather.

00:06:27.160 --> 00:06:29.883
The metal corners on
the case have worn out.

00:06:31.370 --> 00:06:34.960
Daniel uses a special
electricity-conducting pen

00:06:34.960 --> 00:06:36.453
to replate the metal.

00:06:51.550 --> 00:06:56.520
Gerry Gallagher is restoring
a Chanel classic flap bag.

00:06:56.520 --> 00:06:59.683
It was severely burned by
an incandescent light bulb.

00:07:06.910 --> 00:07:09.580
He cuts off only the damaged leather

00:07:09.580 --> 00:07:12.473
in order to preserve
most of the original bag.

00:07:22.870 --> 00:07:25.693
He creates a new piece
with caviar leather.

00:07:45.650 --> 00:07:48.490
He skives the leather
until it's paper thin.

00:07:57.698 --> 00:08:00.360
When he lays the piece onto the bag,

00:08:00.360 --> 00:08:03.110
the transition between
the original leather

00:08:03.110 --> 00:08:05.343
and the new leather is seamless.

00:08:24.170 --> 00:08:26.850
Bag Remake Studio in Shonan, Japan,

00:08:26.850 --> 00:08:29.733
repairs designer bags and accessories.

00:08:31.290 --> 00:08:33.760
The leather on this Louis Vuitton wallet

00:08:33.760 --> 00:08:36.363
has become discolored from heavy use.

00:08:41.780 --> 00:08:44.120
The artist color matches the wallet

00:08:44.120 --> 00:08:46.833
and slowly paints over the faded areas.

00:08:58.600 --> 00:09:01.060
The leather on the edges is peeling

00:09:01.060 --> 00:09:03.883
since it's in the most
commonly touched areas.

00:09:06.500 --> 00:09:08.583
It's sealed using an edge coat.

00:09:11.430 --> 00:09:13.170
This will help to protect the corners

00:09:13.170 --> 00:09:15.483
from further peeling and damage.

00:09:25.350 --> 00:09:29.543
Rio is restoring a pair
of $680 Gucci sneakers.

00:09:32.340 --> 00:09:33.830
The metallic green panel

00:09:33.830 --> 00:09:36.023
on the back of the shoes is peeling.

00:09:37.300 --> 00:09:40.170
Rio uses leather glue and an awl

00:09:40.170 --> 00:09:42.493
to glue the peeled areas back on.

00:09:46.570 --> 00:09:49.070
He also uses a tiny paintbrush

00:09:49.070 --> 00:09:51.803
to fill in faded areas on the panel.

00:09:56.190 --> 00:09:59.010
To finish the job, he
goes over the sneakers

00:09:59.010 --> 00:10:02.172
with white paint to touch
up any scuffed areas.

00:10:02.172 --> 00:10:05.255
(slow ambient music)

